e + N2(X) -> e + N2(W_3Delta_u). Su et al. J. Phys. B 54, 115203 (2021) (CC BY 4.0) below 20 eV; Johnson et al. J. Geophys. Res. 110, A11311 (2005) Table 2 from 20 eV; power-law continuation p = 2.25 above Johnson's last point (to 10 keV). Overlap Su/Johnson: 10 eV 3.17 (+-0.24), 12.5 eV 1.16 (+-0.18), 15 eV 0.82 (+-0.19), 17.5 eV 1.11 (+-0.19), 20 eV 1.09 (+-0.18); step at 20 eV Su/Johnson = 1.09. Continuation share of the rate: T_e 20 eV 0.3 % (zero/hold tail -0.3/+0.1 %), T_e 30 eV 1.2 % (zero/hold tail -1.2/+0.8 %). Header 8.88 eV = experimental vertical excitation energy (Oddershede, Su 2021 Table 1); no threshold shift. Maxwellian-integrated by abep_sim/rate_tables.py (scripts/build_n2_electronic_excitation_tables.py). Reaction set abep-n2n-0.9.
